     a terminal when _f_i_l_d_e_s is not writeable.

     _I_o_c_t_l calls which attempt to modify the state of a process
     control terminal while a process is not in the process group
     of the control terminal will cause a SIGTTOU signal to be
     sent to the process' process group.  Such _i_o_c_t_ls are
     allowed, however, if SIGTTOU is being held, ignored, if the
     process is an orphan which has been inherited by _i_n_i_t, or is
     the child in an incomplete _v_f_o_r_k (see _j_o_b_s(3))

BUGS
     Strictly speaking, since _i_o_c_t_l may be extended in different
     ways to devices with different properties, _a_r_g_p should have
     an open-ended declaration like

          union { struct sgttyb ...; ...  } *argp;

     The important thing is that the size is fixed by `struct
     sgttyb'.

